WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.350
In Tokyo, your checkout page opens in
Japanese with one line still in English.

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.690
Its key went into en.json,
and nobody added it to ja.json.

3
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.620
General Translation lets you stop writing

4
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.870
translation files with
gt-react or gt-next.

5
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.450
Run npx gt init to set up gt-next
and choose your languages.

6
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.770
Write the English inside a T component,
and nobody has to update ja.json by hand.

7
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.530
Then add npx gt translate
to your build script,

8
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.110
and every build writes the Japanese.

9
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.870
Now the tax line appears in Spanish,

10
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.870
French and Japanese with
the rest of the page.
